s soaked in brandy a more  humble alternative was provided by  best-selling author Isabella Beaton she  suggested a toast sandwich literally a  slice of cold toast between two slices  of bread well seasoned with salt and  pepper it was apparently particularly  well-suited for invalids in the 20th  century the British sandwich of two  slices of bread and a filling was joined  by other alternatives from overseas the  Scandinavian open sandwich was praised  by British food writer Marguerite  pattern in the 90  sixties while filled Pitters croissants  and wraps have also crept in to join the  basic bread and butter version toasted  sandwiches came out of the states in the  1920s when the toasty maker was patented  the US had become sandwich Central even  briefly having a national sandwich day  on November the 3rd the original Earl of  Sandwich his birthday but it wasn't  until 1980 that the pre-packed sandwich  made its first appearance in Marks &amp;  Spencer and initially only in five  stores they were an instant hit and now  the working lunch is almost synonymous  with a prawn cocktail sandwich still M&amp;S  is biggest seller the science behind  constructing a non soggy sandwich which  can last all day is very big business  indeed of course the predictable  fillings still vie with slightly more  avant-garde attempts the Sanya which  anyone and many sandwich aficionados  we're blind that the biggest improvement  to any bought sandwich is a layer of  ready salted crisps  you
 

